# Authentication

- Use Better Auth’s official Next.js / React client only. Do not roll a custom JWT client.
- Create a single `authClient` in `lib/auth-client.js` and reuse it (sign-in, sign-out, `useSession`).
- Session and roles come from the server. Canonical roles: `admin`, `manager`, `waiter`, `chef`, `cashier`, `customer`.
- Middleware/layouts may redirect unauthenticated users and hint role-based nav. Backend still enforces every mutation.
- Never persist passwords, tokens, or “isAdmin” flags in `localStorage` as a security control.
- Do not implement Better Auth on this repo as the auth server; that belongs on Express.

```javascript
// lib/auth-client.js
import { createAuthClient } from "better-auth/react";

export const authClient = createAuthClient({
  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
});
```
